// GHSA-pw3x-g8v8-fvj2 (2026-11-19): the built-in `openclaw` tool hands config and plugin changes
// to OpenClaw's setup agent. In a Full Access run those apply with no approval, and they can turn
// on host commands even when exec and file writes are denied. Jorah's `tools.exec.mode: "full"`
// makes its runs Full Access, so this stays after the upgrade to 2026.10.33 too: the fix only adds
// approval for restricted runs. Jorah's config is changed by commit and Adam's yes, never by
// Jorah. The guard also lists `openclaw` as blocked (config/permission-matrix.json).
// Global denies can't be granted back per agent. Name, not group: `group:openclaw` would also
// remove message, automations and other tools Jorah uses.
// Measured on live before this: main was offered the tool in 2 of 143 claude-cli sessions
// (2026-11-17 on jorah-dev, 2026-11-19 on live) and never called it (docs/runbooks/jorah-on-pc.md).
// Undo: the same patch without "openclaw".
{
  tools: { deny: ["nodes", "computer", "gateway", "openclaw"] },
}
